WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.527
Advanced SQL is mostly about controlling intermediate results and row context.

00:00:05.527 --> 00:00:09.962
A CTE gives a meaningful name to a stage in the query.

00:00:09.962 --> 00:00:16.547
A window function lets one row see related rows without automatically collapsing the result.

00:00:16.547 --> 00:00:19.812
Sequence functions depend on a meaningful order.

00:00:19.812 --> 00:00:21.512
And throughout the module, grain still matters.

00:00:21.512 --> 00:00:26.942
At every stage, you should be able to complete the sentence: one row represents what?

00:00:26.942 --> 00:00:34.207
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:34.207 --> 00:00:38.422
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:38.422 --> 00:00:42.767
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:49.162
In a real setting such as a sales team calculating running revenue and top products by region,

00:00:49.162 --> 00:00:55.342
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:55.342 --> 00:00:57.582
before discussing syntax.

00:00:57.582 --> 00:01:03.817
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
